       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum daily dose for adults (3,200 mg/day under medical supervision). That much raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **400 mg four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a common upper-range regimen\n- **1,600 mg/day** divided in some other way\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give the clinical rationale. I'd still suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
